<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 15px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # Introducing Panama to the World – Lesson # 3</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.1em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 3</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Speaking</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Grade:</b> 12th Grade (CEFR: B1.3)</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Scenario:</b> International Communication</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Theme:</b> Introducing Panama to the World</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Speaking: Productive: Present a summary of various content including products, entertainment, or recreational activities. Interactive: Debate on topics relevant to current social trends.</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Speaking: Can summarize content that highlights Panama's cultural identity, innovations, or contributions as part of introducing the country to the world (e.g., "It is said that Panama has been praised for its efforts in preserving biodiversity.") Can participate in debates on issues related to Panama's national and global significance, presenting clear and well-supported arguments (e.g., "The Panama Canal's expansion has greatly boosted global trade efficiency, which I argue strengthens Panama's position in the international economy.") Can answer questions during a debate, defending or expanding on their argument about the importance of English proficiency to effectively communicate Panama's significance as a global trade location (e.g., "Panama's position as a key trade hub requires clear communication in English to engage international partners and promote economic growth.")</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="background-color: #f2f2f2;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; text-align: left; width: 33%;"><h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0;">Stage & Description</h3></th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; text-align: left; width: 34%;"><h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0;">Activities & Teacher Actions</h3></th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; text-align: left; width: 33%;"><h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0;">Estimated Date and Time</h3></th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task (Engagement, Modeling and Clarification)</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">This stage aims to activate prior knowledge, introduce the speaking task, and set the context for international communication about Panama.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays a world map and points to Panama. Students work in pairs to brainstorm and share two reasons why Panama is considered a "global hub" for international trade. They then share their ideas with the class. (e.g., "The Panama Canal is a key transit route for global shipping.")</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models phrases for introducing a topic and expressing opinions respectfully, relevant to the theme "Introducing Panama to the World." For example, "Panama is recognized for its trade influence, which has a significant impact on global commerce." and "From my perspective, Panama's biodiversity is a valuable asset that must be protected." The teacher emphasizes the pronunciation of /t/ in "trade" and /g/ in "global," and models stressing modal verbs in sentences like "You MUST be proficient in English to engage internationally."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If I say 'Panama is recognized for its trade influence,' am I saying Panama *does* the recognizing, or *is* recognized by others?" (Expected answer: Is recognized by others.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"When I say 'We MUST ensure clear communication,' does 'must' mean it's optional or absolutely necessary?" (Expected answer: Absolutely necessary.)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "International Communication".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> An audio recording of a short (approx. 2-3 minute) panel discussion or interview segment titled "Panama's Role in Global Commerce and Biodiversity Conservation." The genre is an informative discussion, register is professional, and format is audio-visual (if possible, with a transcript provided for reference). The segment includes experts discussing the Panama Canal, financial services, and efforts to protect biodiversity, using the target grammar (passive voice, modals of necessity, relative clauses) and vocabulary (trade, global, biodiversity, hub, relevant, impact, maintain, sustainable).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Engage in conversations about Panama's role in global trade: "Why is the Panama Canal important for international trade?" Lead presentations on Panama's global role, ensuring all viewpoints are acknowledged and effectively communicated.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist questions:</b> "What are the two main areas of Panama's global significance discussed by the panelists?" (Expected answer: Global trade and biodiversity/ecological significance.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False:</b> Students listen and determine if statements are true or false, correcting the false ones. Examples: "The Panama Canal's expansion is considered to have negatively impacted global trade efficiency." (False: greatly boosted). "Panama is recognized mainly for its financial services sector, not its natural protected areas." (False: for both).</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Speaking.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students will practice using the passive voice to introduce Panama's role, modals of necessity in professional settings, and relative clauses to add information. Target vocabulary includes: <i>recognize, attract, maintain, impact, emphasize, require, engage, global, key, critical, proficient, sustainable, strategic, significant, necessary, valuable</i>.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Controlled Practice (Sentence Transformation - Passive Voice):</b> Teacher provides active sentences about Panama's global role. Students work individually to transform them into passive voice, then read their sentences aloud. (e.g., Teacher: "Many countries praise Panama for its efforts in preserving biodiversity." Student: "Panama is praised for its efforts in preserving biodiversity.")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Semi-controlled Practice (Modal Chain Drill - necessity/obligation):</b> Students work in small groups. The teacher starts a sentence using a modal of necessity (must/should), and the first student completes it, then starts a new sentence for the next student, incorporating another target vocabulary word. (e.g., Teacher: "Panamanian professionals must..." Student 1: "...be proficient in English to engage international partners." Student 1 then prompts: "Our country should...")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Pair Interaction (Debate Starters - Relative Clauses and Pragmatic Expressions):</b> Students are given cards with half-sentences requiring a relative clause and a prompt for a debate. They complete the sentence and engage in a short debate using expressions for showing respect for different opinions. (e.g., Card: "The Panama Canal, which..." Prompt: "...is a major route for trade, needs further expansion." Partner B responds: "From my perspective, expanding the Canal further might lead to..."). They practice stressing Wh- question words in their follow-up questions (e.g., "WHAT MAKES Panama a KEY player...?").</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "International Communication."</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Structured Debate and Summary Presentation. Students work in groups of four to prepare for a debate on "The most effective strategies for introducing Panama's global relevance to international companies and ecotourists." Two students will argue for one strategy (e.g., emphasizing trade and financial services), and the other two will argue for another (e.g., emphasizing biodiversity and cultural customs). Each group must incorporate all target grammar structures and at least 8-10 target vocabulary words in their arguments. During the debate, students must engage interactively, present clear and well-supported arguments, and answer questions while defending or expanding on their arguments. After the debate, each group will collaboratively present a summary of the key arguments and their conclusions to the class.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to Theme/Scenario:</b> This activity directly simulates a professional setting where Panamanian representatives (students) must communicate effectively to introduce and promote their country's significance to an international audience, using English as the primary communication tool. It requires critical thinking about Panama's contributions and the best ways to present them.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher Role:</b> Facilitates group formation, provides clear instructions and a rubric, circulates to monitor and provide support, observes use of target language, and acts as moderator during the debates and question-and-answer sessions.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students participate in the group debate and deliver their summary presentation. The teacher uses an observation checklist/rubric to assess individual and group performance.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Intelligible pronunciation (especially /t/, /g/, stressed modals/Wh- questions).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Accurate and appropriate use of target vocabulary (e.g., <i>trade, biodiversity, hub, proficient, strategic</i>).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Correct application of passive voice, modals of necessity, and relative clauses.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity and coherence of arguments and summary presentation.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Active and respectful collaboration within the group and during the debate (pragmatic and sociolinguistic competence).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Ability to defend or expand on arguments when questioned.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete a short reflection form before leaving.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How effectively did I use specific vocabulary and grammar structures to introduce Panama's global significance during the debate?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was one new way I learned to express my opinion respectfully during a discussion about a controversial topic?"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was the most challenging part of debating or summarizing Panama's role, and how did using English help or hinder my communication?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How can I improve my ability to present strong, clear arguments about Panama's contributions in future international communication scenarios?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What worked well in this speaking-focused lesson? Were students actively engaged in using the target grammar and vocabulary in meaningful conversations?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What adjustments or scaffolds are needed for the next lesson (Writing)? Perhaps more guided practice on sentence construction with relative clauses, or specific phrases for connecting ideas in written arguments?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson in the theme sequence:</b> This speaking lesson has solidified students' oral command of vocabulary and grammar related to introducing Panama. The next lesson (Lesson 4: Writing Composition) will build upon this by having students formally write persuasive paragraphs or a short essay, summarizing and arguing for Panama's global significance, directly applying the language practiced orally today into a written format. This will involve constructing well-structured sentences with passive voice, modals of necessity, and relative clauses, and using the practiced vocabulary to develop their written arguments about Panama's role as a global hub for trade and biodiversity.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>